<title>USA: MBIA qualifies eight bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies eight bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp. on Wednesday said it qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues slated for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Hollister, S.D., Calif., General Obligations (GOs), $3.3 million.</p>
<p>--Santa Clara, U.S.D., Calif, GOs, $50 million.</p>
<p>--Sunapee, S.D., N.H., GOs, $4.054 million.</p>
<p>--Norwood, N.J., General Improvment, $2.778 million.</p>
<p>--Canandaiqua, N.Y., $1.578 million public improvement</p>
<p>--Royalton C.S.D., NY., $9.002 million.</p>
<p>--University of Houston Board of Regents, Tex., Revenues, $5.15 million.</p>
<p>--Amery, Wis., $1.61 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
